cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use FaunaLapse in your research, please cite the software using the metadata provided below."
title: "FaunaLapse: a smartphone application for scheduled time-lapse monitoring of insects and other animals"
abstract: >-
  FaunaLapse is an offline Android application that turns old or low-cost phones
  into time-lapse cameras watching one spot, for example pollinators visiting a
  flower. It records short photo bursts or video clips on a daily schedule with the
  screen off, keeps only a user-chosen square region of interest, and closes the
  camera between bursts to save energy and limit heat, so a phone can run for days
  on a power bank. Every photo and event is logged together with field metadata
  named after the Camtrap DP standard for camera traps, so visit rates can be
  computed later. The application uses no artificial intelligence and runs on
  Android 7.0 or newer.
type: software
license: AGPL-3.0-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/valentinitnelav/fauna-lapse"
version: "0.1.0-alpha.1"
# TODO (owner): add the day of the GitHub release, for example:
# date-released: "2026-10-20"
keywords:
  - pollinators
  - pollination ecology
  - time-lapse
  - camera trap
  - Camtrap DP
  - insect monitoring
  - pollinator monitoring
  - biodiversity monitoring
  - smartphone
  - Android
  - low-cost
